# LeadKart compose-stack environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `docker/.env` and fill the required values. The
# compose.yml uses `${VAR:?missing ...}` substitution so missing
# values fail at `docker compose up` time rather than runtime.
#
# DO NOT commit `docker/.env` — see .gitignore. The literal values
# below are placeholders that the application's secrets validator
# (internal/platform/config/validate.go) will REJECT at boot via
# substring-match against `placeholderMarkers`. That's intentional:
# operators MUST supply real values; the dev experience is "compose
# refuses to start until you populate this file" rather than "API
# silently boots with an attacker-known dev key."

# ---- Postgres -----------------------------------------------------
# leadkart_app role DSN (the application's runtime role; goose runs
# under the owner role inside the migrate container). Override only
# when pointing the stack at an external Postgres.
# LEADKART_POSTGRES__DSN=postgres://leadkart:leadkart_dev@postgres:5432/leadkart?sslmode=disable

# ---- JWT signing --------------------------------------------------
# Generate a fresh 32-byte (≥256-bit) random key. Examples:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#   head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64
LEADKART_JWT__KEY_ID=k1-dev
LEADKART_JWT__SIGNING_KEY=REPLACE_ME_WITH_A_FRESH_RANDOM_KEY_NEVER_REUSE_ACROSS_ENVS
